WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.000
2001's "The Fast and the Furious" found major&nbsp;
success by all accounts, and in the years since,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.040
the franchise it spawned has more than left its&nbsp;
mark on Hollywood. It has made several big-screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.400
stars, taken in boatloads of money, — over $6&nbsp;
billion, in fact — and made front-page news on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.720
more than one occasion. One of the strongest&nbsp;
examples of this phenomenon is the bitter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:26.400
feud between two of the series' biggest names, Vin&nbsp;
Diesel and Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson. It took hold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.760
of the media several years ago, and has seemingly&nbsp;
reemerged on the road to the premiere of "F9."

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.280
In an interview with Men's Health,&nbsp;
Diesel was asked about his experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.840
working with Johnson in previous "Fast and&nbsp;
Furious" installments. More specifically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.320
he discussed the part he played in influencing&nbsp;
Johnson's performance as Luke Hobbs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.560
Diesel said, noting that he went the extra&nbsp;
mile to make Hobbs come off as an in-your-face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.000
hard-hitting character. and that&nbsp;
he's proud of the final product,

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.080
"My approach at the time was a lot of tough&nbsp;
love to assist in getting that performance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.360
where it needed to be. I would do&nbsp;
anything I'd have to do in order&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.920
to get performances in anything I'm producing."

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.400
At first glance, this may&nbsp;
just sound like Vin Diesel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:09.280
explaining an unorthodox method to get Dwayne&nbsp;
Johnson's portrayal of Luke Hobbs just right.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.440
But when you consider their personal&nbsp;
history and various reports from their time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:17.920
working on "Fast and Furious" films&nbsp;
together, Diesel's 2021 statement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.640
is completely recontextualized. Buckle up,&nbsp;
let’s ride through their rocky relationship.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.720
This story begins on August 8th, 2016, when&nbsp;
Johnson made a since-deleted Instagram post&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.520
to voice his displeasure with someone on the&nbsp;
"Fate of the Furious" set. He outed an unnamed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:37.360
person for acting unprofessional&nbsp;
and not backing up their behavior,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:42.080
clarifying that he was on good terms with&nbsp;
most of the cast and crew otherwise. He wrote,

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.040
"When you watch this movie next&nbsp;
April and it seems like I'm not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.440
acting in some of these scenes and my&nbsp;
blood is legit boiling—you're right."

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.040
Naturally, this opened up speculation&nbsp;
over who he's referring to.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:57.200
Even more naturally, various news outlets&nbsp;
ran with this developing story and spread&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:02.400
the common belief that Vin Diesel was the person&nbsp;
Johnson was not-so-subtly pointing the finger at.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:08.640
According to TMZ, the two parties met up for a&nbsp;
“secret meeting” on August 9th, 2016, in hopes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.040
of putting their anger to rest, adding that&nbsp;
the "Fate of the Furious" cast was unhappy with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:18.160
Johnson for causing a stir at the tail end of the&nbsp;
shoot. Apparently, the clash stemmed from Diesel's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:23.440
position as a producer and his penchant for&nbsp;
making changes that drew the ire of his co-star.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:28.000
Later, an anonymous source close to the project&nbsp;
told People that the tension between the actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.160
had been on the rise for months. A common&nbsp;
complaint was Johnson's apparent lack of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:37.280
punctuality, sometimes not appearing at all&nbsp;
and stalling production. This angered Diesel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.000
but he was far from absolved of any wrongdoing.&nbsp;
Other reports claimed he would engage in similar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.240
behavior, even locking himself in his&nbsp;
trailer during the filming of "Furious 7."

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.960
As word of the budding rivalry began to spread,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.120
Johnson hopped back on Instagram to try&nbsp;
and quell any further rumors about him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:57.840
Diesel, or anyone else connected to the "Fast&nbsp;
and Furious" name. Once again addressing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:02.960
on-set animosity but highlighting that the&nbsp;
ability to work past it is what really matters.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.400
"And like with any team – that's a&nbsp;
family – there's gonna be conflict.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.320
Family is gonna have differences of&nbsp;
opinion and fundamental core beliefs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.560
To me, conflict can be a good thing,&nbsp;
when its followed by great resolution."

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:19.200
Come August 19th, Vin Diesel took to&nbsp;
Facebook to speak directly on the subject,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.360
showing his appreciation for the fans for&nbsp;
their support and letting them know that,

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:25.840
"Without you, I would not be doing Fast 8."

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:30.800
He then detailed their involvement in Johnson&nbsp;
landing the Hobbs role, to begin with, revealing,

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:33.840
"We gave the role that was originally&nbsp;
written for Tommy Lee Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.320
we gave it to Dwayne, and he shined in it."

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:39.920
It seems all that “sunny” chatter&nbsp;
didn’t make it all the way to Johnson.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:43.600
He made a post of his own that same&nbsp;
day on Instagram. He announced he'd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:47.600
wrapped up on "The Fate of the Furious"&nbsp;
with a caption thanking numerous people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:52.800
involved in making the project a reality.&nbsp;
Guess who he didn’t mention? Yup: Vin Diesel.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:57.440
Though few doubted Johnson and Diesel weren't at&nbsp;
odds, their fellow "Fate of the Furious" star,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:02.480
Michelle Rodriguez, set the record&nbsp;
straight. She told People in September 2016:

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:05.200
"Any human being who knows what&nbsp;
men are like knows to stay out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:08.240
[of those] situations and let them figure it out."

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:11.600
Nevertheless, she clarified that the&nbsp;
two were friends even in the face of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:16.800
their heated conflict and would put aside&nbsp;
their differences sooner rather than later.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:20.480
Months later, the press tour for "Fate&nbsp;
of the Furious" was in full swing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:27.200
and Diesel expressed his love and appreciation&nbsp;
for Johnson. He told USA Today on April 7th, 2017,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.920
"I don't think the world really&nbsp;
realizes how close we are,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.640
in a weird way. In my house, he's Uncle Dwayne."

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:37.520
Two days later on Entertainment Tonight, Johnson&nbsp;
posited that his issues with Diesel boiled down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:41.440
to "different philosophies" and that the&nbsp;
most important thing at that juncture was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:46.160
the film itself. With that, TMZ reported&nbsp;
on April 18th that the two were once again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:49.360
on good terms and that their&nbsp;
beef was officially squashed.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.240
With all of this backstory in&nbsp;
mind, could Vin Diesel's most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:56.320
recent quip about "The Rock" and his&nbsp;
acting abilities reopen old wounds?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:00.720
You can bet that Johnson’s cooking up a response&nbsp;
for sure - we can practically smell it now.

